From: Gabriel Lafond-Thenaille <gabriel@videolabs.io>
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: preserve lib prefix when cross-compiling for Windows

ggml clears CMAKE_STATIC_LIBRARY_PREFIX unconditionally on WIN32,
which strips the "lib" prefix from ggml-base.a, ggml-cpu.a, etc.
when cross-compiling from Linux.  This breaks pkg-config consumers
that reference those libraries as -lggml-base etc.

Restrict the prefix removal to native Windows builds only.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@
 endif()
 
 # remove the lib prefix on win32 mingw
-if (WIN32)
+if (WIN32 AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
     set(CMAKE_STATIC_LIBRARY_PREFIX "")
     set(CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX "")
     set(CMAKE_SHARED_MODULE_PREFIX  "")
